{"s001":"Skip to story","s002":"Manas stands before his mounted companions and the Ala-Too mountains, in three independently moving illustrated layers.","s003":"A people. A hero. An eternal story.","s004":"MANAS","s005":"The epic of the Kyrgyz hero.","s006":"Born of the mountains. Bound by courage.","s007":"Discover the legend that became the soul","s008":"of a people.","s009":"Enter the epic","s010":"ALA-TOO · KYRGYZSTAN · AN ENDURING SPIRIT","s011":"SCROLL TO DISCOVER","s012":"He was a grey-maned wolf.","s013":"Tribes.","s014":"One people.","s015":"Generations.","s016":"One legacy.","s017":"An oral tradition.","s018":"A living heritage.","s019":"UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage","s020":"Inscribed in 2013","s021":"The beginning","s022":"A prayer.","s023":"A birth.","s024":"A destiny.","s025":"Before there was a hero, there was a father’s longing. Far from their ancestral homeland, Zhakyp and Chyiyrdy waited for a child.","s026":"Then came Manas. His birth carried the promise of a different future: a scattered people finding their way home, and a boy growing into the courage they needed.","s027":"No hero stands alone","s028":"Zhakyp at the doorway of a Kyrgyz yurt, with a cradle in its warmly lit interior.","s029":"Where a people’s hope began","s030":"Жаралуу · I","s031":"The fellowship","s032":"Forty hearts.","s033":"One banner.","s034":"Strength was never his alone. The forty comrades embody loyalty, courage, and the bonds that hold a people together. Meet three warriors and the elder who guides them.","s035":"Companions of Manas","s036":"01 / THE WARRIOR","s037":"Illustrated portrait of Almambet in chainmail and a crimson mantle, holding a spear.","s038":"Almambet","s039":"The sworn brother","s040":"02 / THE WARRIOR","s041":"Illustrated portrait of Chubak in fur-trimmed armor with a round shield.","s042":"Chubak","s043":"The fearless heart","s044":"03 / THE WARRIOR","s045":"Illustrated portrait of Syrgak, a young scout in chainmail and an indigo mantle.","s046":"Syrgak","s047":"The trusted companion","s048":"04 / THE COUNSELOR","s049":"Illustrated portrait of Bakai, the white-bearded counselor in a felt kalpak.","s050":"Bakai","s051":"The voice of wisdom","s052":"КЫРК ЧОРО · THE FORTY COMRADES","s053":"FORTY INDIVIDUALS. AN UNBROKEN BOND.","s054":"Forty symbolic warrior badges","s055":"Each badge marks a place in the fellowship. The names and episodes vary across the epic’s oral versions.","s056":"Enable JavaScript to explore the companion profiles and forty-badge gallery.","s057":"Battles & belonging","s058":"For the land.","s059":"For each other.","s060":"Across the steppe, Manas faces the Qalmaq and other adversaries of the epic. Beyond the clash of armies lies a greater purpose: bringing his people together.","s061":"Manas and his mounted companions gather beneath their crimson banners.","s062":"A homeland is more","s063":"than a place.","s064":"Kanykey in a white elechek and crimson embroidered coat, holding a folded textile.","s065":"Courage has many forms","s066":"Kanykey.","s067":"The strength beside him.","s068":"Wise and resourceful, Kanikey is central to the story. Her marriage to Manas joins their destinies; her care and foresight help sustain his companions.","s069":"When his story ends, she protects their son Semetei — and carries its future forward.","s070":"The epic holds triumph and loss together. The Great Campaign tests loyalty, exacts a terrible cost, and leaves the next generation with an unfinished task.","s071":"An episode in four panels","s072":"A feast.","s073":"A clash of legends.","s074":"At Kökötöy’s memorial feast, heroes gather to honor the dead and test the living. Among the contests: a charged encounter between Manas and Qongurbay.","s075":"Select a panel to see the full illustration and read its story.","s076":"The duel at Kökötöy’s feast, read in numbered order","s077":"A vast gathering of white yurts and mounted guests around a tournament ground in the mountain steppe.","s078":"The gathering.","s079":"Across the steppe, guests arrive for Kökötöy’s memorial feast. Rival heroes share one field.","s080":"Expand panel 1: The gathering","s081":"Read panel","s082":"Manas in crimson and Qongurbay in indigo face one another on horseback with their lances ready.","s083":"The challenge.","s084":"Manas and Qongurbay take their places. Between them, a stretch of earth. Around them, a waiting crowd.","s085":"Expand panel 2: The challenge","s086":"The two mounted warriors charge through dust; their lances cross as Manas strikes Qongurbay’s armor.","s087":"THE CLASH","s088":"A heartbeat. A thunder of hooves.","s089":"The riders close. Lances cross. Manas’s strike finds its mark.","s090":"Expand panel 3: The clash","s091":"Manas steadies his horse as dust settles, with his opponent riding toward the distant gathering.","s092":"The dust settles.","s093":"The contest passes into memory. The rivalry carries on — and so does the epic.","s094":"Expand panel 4: The dust settles","s095":"Inside the episode","s096":"A gathering of rivals","s097":"The memorial feast is a setting for remembrance and games. Heroes who oppose one another elsewhere in the epic meet on the same contest ground, with Manas presiding.","s098":"Two names, one opponent","s099":"Qongurbay is also rendered as Konurbay in English. The spellings reflect different ways of representing the name; here, both refer to Manas’s rival.","s100":"From voice to picture","s101":"This sequence is a visual adaptation. The recorded episode includes their joust and Manas’s lance strike. The framing, pauses, colors, and captions are our interpretation of that encounter.","s102":"A visual retelling with original captions, inspired by the memorial-feast episode. Oral versions vary.","s103":"Explore the episode’s source ↗","s104":"Another story from the feast","s105":"A second story from the feast","s106":"Wisdom meets strength","s107":"The elder and the giant","s108":"An impossible rival.","s109":"An unexpected strength.","s110":"At the same great feast, another contest unfolds. This time, the story belongs to an elder, a giant — and the woman whose foresight changes everything.","s111":"Four moments. One extraordinary reversal. Select a panel to enter the story.","s112":"Koshoy and Joloy’s wrestling match, read in numbered order","s113":"Elder Koshoy in an ochre coat faces the towering wrestler Joloy before a crowd on the mountain steppe.","s114":"The elder steps forward.","s115":"Joloy towers over the field. The one who answers his challenge is the white-bearded Koshoy.","s116":"Expand panel 1: The elder steps forward","s117":"Kanykey in a white elechek and crimson embroidered coat sews reinforced leather trousers inside a yurt.","s118":"A strength made by hand.","s119":"Before the contest, Kanykey has already prepared something extraordinary: the kandagai, sturdy leather wrestling trousers.","s120":"Expand panel 2: A strength made by hand","s121":"Koshoy raises his open palms in blessing before Kanykey, with yurts and mountains behind them.","s122":"A blessing for the future.","s123":"The trousers fit. Before he wrestles, Koshoy blesses their maker — and names a hoped-for son: Semetey.","s124":"Expand panel 3: A blessing for the future","s125":"White-bearded Koshoy in ochre leather trousers throws the larger Joloy through a swirl of dust.","s126":"THE TURN","s127":"The impossible turns.","s128":"Exhaustion nearly wins. Manas calls out. Koshoy rallies, finds his footing, and throws the giant.","s129":"Expand panel 4: The impossible turns","s130":"The story behind the contest","s131":"The kandagai","s132":"Kanykey’s leather trousers have room hidden in their seams. Let out, they fit Koshoy. Her care becomes part of his strength.","s133":"A future spoken aloud","s134":"Koshoy’s blessing comes before the match. It links this episode to Semetey, whose story follows his father’s in the epic trilogy.","s135":"The sewing scene imagines the preparation behind the garment. These four images compress a much longer encounter; their framing and captions are an original visual interpretation.","s136":"Inspired by the wrestling episode in the prose retelling of Kökötöy’s feast. Oral versions vary.","s137":"The garment & blessing ↗","s138":"The wrestling match ↗","s139":"The future she must protect","s140":"After the fall of Manas","s141":"A future carried forward","s142":"Kanykey’s flight to Bukhara","s143":"Across the wilderness.","s144":"For one small life.","s145":"After Manas’s death, Kanykey and his mother, Chiyrdy, carry his infant son toward safety — through hardship, unexpected kindness, and a moment of wonder.","s146":"Follow the journey in four panels. Open each illustration for the full story.","s147":"Kanykey’s flight to Bukhara, read in numbered order","s148":"Kanykey carries swaddled Semetey while elderly Chiyrdy walks beside her across the stony steppe at dusk.","s149":"The road out of Talas.","s150":"After Manas’s death, Kanykey and Chiyrdy flee with baby Semetey. A dangerous journey is his chance to live.","s151":"Expand panel 1: The road out of Talas","s152":"Bakai carries Semetey safely above the river as he leads a horse bearing Kanykey and Chiyrdy through the current.","s153":"A friend at the river.","s154":"The Syr Darya blocks their way. Bakai finds them, carries Semetey, and helps the women across.","s155":"Expand panel 2: A friend at the river","s156":"A white argali ewe stands beside Semetey’s cradle beneath a tree while Kanykey and Chiyrdy sleep nearby.","s157":"A guardian in white.","s158":"At sacred Bayterek, a white argali ewe nourishes the child. In the wilderness, help takes an extraordinary form.","s159":"Expand panel 3: A guardian in white","s160":"Beside an orchard pool, Kanykey gently hands baby Semetey to her brother Ismail, with Chiyrdy beside her.","s161":"A future kept alive.","s162":"Her brother Ismail recognizes the travelers. Kanykey entrusts Semetey to him; Bukhara becomes the child’s refuge.","s163":"Expand panel 4: A future kept alive","s164":"Inside the journey","s165":"Two generations of courage","s166":"Kanykey travels with Chiyrdy, Manas’s mother. Their shared task is to protect Semetey. This chapter moves the epic’s attention from the warrior to the people who preserve his future.","s167":"The white argali","s168":"In this retelling, a female wild mountain sheep feeds Semetey at Bayterek and disappears when Kanykey approaches. Our illustration imagines its arrival beside the cradle.","s169":"A childhood in Bukhara","s170":"Ismail, Kanykey’s brother, takes the child into his care. The family conceals Semetey’s parentage. The story of who he is — and where he belongs — still lies ahead.","s171":"Adapted from Z. Bektenov and K. Nanaev’s prose retelling. These four moments condense a longer journey; oral versions vary.","s172":"Read the flight episode ↗","s173":"The white argali passage ↗","s174":"The child becomes the next chapter","s175":"The legacy","s176":"A story too great","s177":"for one lifetime.","s178":"Father. Son. Grandson. Three connected epics follow a legacy of belonging through separation, return, and renewal.","s179":"I · THE FATHER","s180":"Manas in his crimson cape and chainmail.","s181":"Manas","s182":"The unifier. A hero whose strength gathers a scattered people, and whose struggles become their shared memory.","s183":"The courage to begin","s184":"II · THE SON","s185":"Semetey in a gold mantle and pointed helmet.","s186":"Semetey","s187":"The inheritor. Raised away from his father’s homeland, Semetei returns to Talas to reclaim his place and continue the story.","s188":"The courage to return","s189":"III · THE GRANDSON","s190":"Seytek in ivory and indigo, wearing a white felt kalpak.","s191":"Seytek","s192":"The restorer. A new generation confronts old divisions, seeking justice and a renewed peace among the Kyrgyz.","s193":"The courage to renew","s194":"An illustrated Kyrgyz manaschi wearing a white kalpak, reciting with an expressive raised hand inside a yurt.","s195":"A voice becomes a world","s196":"Манасчылар · VIII","s197":"The living voice","s198":"Not written in stone.","s199":"Carried in the voice.","s200":"Breath becomes rhythm. A gesture becomes a galloping horse. In the voice of a manaschi, the epic lives again.","s201":"Great reciters such as Sagymbai Orozbakov and Sayakbay Karalaev preserved expansive versions of the story. Today, new voices continue this living tradition.","s202":"Watch and hear the Manas tradition in a UNESCO film","s203":"HEAR THE LIVING EPIC","s204":"UNESCO · Aitysh Film · 09:57","s205":"A documentary with recitation in Kyrgyz. Opens a video player; internet required.","s206":"Manas is traditionally recited without instrumental accompaniment.","s207":"The forty tribes united","s208":"The forty tribes.","s209":"United.","s210":"ROOTED IN KYRGYZSTAN. SHARED WITH THE WORLD.","s211":"About & sources","s212":"Back to the beginning ↑","s213":"Story, symbols & credits +","s214":"This is an artistic introduction to a living oral epic, not a definitive text. Episodes, names, and interpretations differ between reciters. The forty badges symbolize the fellowship rather than a fixed roster. Illustrations are original AI-generated interpretations, not historical portraits.","s215":"The ornament system draws on the tündük (yurt crown), kochkor müyüz (ram’s horns), kerege (yurt lattice), and tumar (triangular amulet). The sun-and-tündük emblem uses the supplied icon; the other SVG ornaments are contemporary interpretations of these forms. Felt textures and paired scrolling motifs reference Kyrgyz shyrdak craft.","s216":"Explore the sources:","s217":"UNESCO — Manas, Semetey, Seytek","s218":"UNESCO — Ala-kiyiz and Shyrdak","s219":"Silk Road Foundation — Introduction to Manas","s220":"UNESCO — The Kyrgyz epic Manas","s221":"Story navigation","s222":"Open chapter guide","s223":"Next chapter: The fellowship","s224":"Pause decorative motion","s225":"Pause motion","s226":"Close chapter guide","s227":"Your journey through the epic","s228":"Every chapter.","s229":"A world to discover.","s230":"All story chapters","s231":"The duel","s232":"The elder & the giant","s233":"The flight to Bukhara","s234":"Choose a chapter, or let the story unfold as you scroll.","s235":"Close companion profile","s236":"Kökötöy’s memorial feast","s237":"Panel 01 / 04","s238":"Close comic reader","s239":"Swipe the artwork to turn the page.","s240":"Look closer","s241":"Read about the source episode ↗","s242":"Previous comic panel","s243":"Previous","s244":"Choose comic panel","s245":"Panel 1: The gathering","s246":"Panel 2: The challenge","s247":"Panel 3: The clash","s248":"Panel 4: The dust settles","s249":"Next comic panel","s250":"Next","s251":"Close video","s252":"The living voice of Manas","s253":"UNESCO · Aitysh Film, 2013. If the player is unavailable,","s254":"watch the film on YouTube ↗","s255":"Symbolic comrade {number} of 40","s256":"Panel {number} / {total}","s257":"Panel {number}: {title}","s258":"Panel {number} of {total}: {title}","s259":"Next chapter: {title}","s260":"Almambet is one of Manas’s closest companions and an accomplished warrior. His journey from another community into Manas’s fellowship makes their bond especially powerful. Alongside Syrgak, he undertakes dangerous reconnaissance during the Great Campaign. His story joins extraordinary loyalty with the pain of leaving one home to find another.","s261":"A formidable warrior and a prominent companion of Manas, Chubak brings fierce courage to the fellowship. The epic also gives him pride and rivalry: even heroes must learn what loyalty asks of them. His encounters with Almambet reveal the human tensions within a legendary brotherhood.","s262":"Syrgak is remembered among Manas’s brave companions. He joins Almambet on reconnaissance in the Great Campaign, where endurance and trust matter as much as force. His place in the epic reminds us that a great undertaking depends on those willing to stand beside one another.","s263":"Bakai is the wise elder and counselor whose experience helps guide Manas. He offers judgment amid the passions of warriors and remains a thread of continuity across generations. Presented here alongside the comrades, he represents another kind of strength: the patience to advise, remember, and protect a people’s future.","s264":"UNESCO: Kyrgyz epic trilogy — Manas, Semetey, Seytek","s265":"The gathering","s266":"Remembrance becomes a meeting ground","s267":"Heroes arrive for Kökötöy’s memorial feast, where remembrance is joined by games. Manas presides over the gathering.","s268":"Our opening panel lets the crowd fill the horizon. Yurts, riders, and banners frame an open space: for a moment, the field holds both hospitality and the possibility of conflict.","s269":"Follow the line of spectators toward the center. The red mantle identifies Manas, while the distant indigo figure introduces his opponent before the closer encounter.","s270":"The challenge","s271":"Two riders. One field.","s272":"The feast brings Manas and Qongurbay into a mounted contest. Their joust is one of the episode’s encounters.","s273":"The second panel stretches the moment before contact. The long diagonal lances nearly meet across the empty sky; the horses and riders form opposing shapes. The tension comes from the distance still left between them.","s274":"Crimson and indigo are visual cues for the two riders in this adaptation. The empty space between the lance points gives the approaching collision its direction.","s275":"The clash","s276":"The decisive instant","s277":"Manas’s lance strike against Qongurbay is the central event represented here.","s278":"The illustration compresses the charge into one moment. Flying fabric, crossing lances, and thrown-up dust pull the eye toward the impact. The crowd recedes as the two riders dominate the scene.","s279":"Trace the lances from the riders’ hands toward the center. The composition turns the weapons into crossing lines, while the horses’ movement carries the action across the page.","s280":"The dust settles","s281":"A pause in a much larger story","s282":"Our final panel imagines a breath after the clash: lowered weapons, settling dust, and the gathering coming back into view.","s283":"This quiet closing image is an artistic transition rather than a quoted passage. It invites the reader to look beyond a single feat of strength and return to the people watching — the community that will remember and retell the story.","s284":"Compare this panel with the first. The crowded field returns, but the viewpoint is closer. Manas’s lowered lance and the retreating figure change the rhythm from motion to stillness.","s286":"The elder steps forward","s288":"A challenge no one can ignore","s289":"Joloy calls for a wrestler. The warriors hesitate; Manas’s strengths lie in mounted combat. Elder Koshoy agrees to face the giant.","s290":"This opening image makes the imbalance visible. One figure seems to occupy the whole sky. Across the empty ground, a white beard and a steady gaze answer him. The crowd can only watch.","s292":"The contrasting silhouettes make this a contest of scale before a hand is raised. Koshoy’s ochre clothing distinguishes him from Joloy’s indigo throughout the sequence.","s293":"A strength made by hand","s294":"Earlier, inside the yurt","s295":"Koshoy needs trousers strong enough for wrestling. Kanykey’s kandagai are brought forward; hidden seam allowances are opened until the garment fits.","s296":"Our imagined flashback slows the story to the movement of a needle. Warm felt, leather, and careful hands replace the noise of the field. Kanykey’s preparation gives the contest another kind of hero.","s297":"The white elechek and crimson coat connect Kanykey to her earlier portrait. The garment, rather than a weapon, is the focal point: something made with foresight, ready when it is needed.","s298":"A blessing for the future","s299":"Before the first hold","s300":"Grateful to Kanykey, Koshoy gives her a blessing before the bout. He speaks of the son she longs for and names him Semetey.","s301":"The open palms create a quiet pause between preparation and struggle. This scene looks beyond the tournament: the next generation enters the story as a hope, long before it appears as a hero.","s302":"The blessing is placed before the wrestling victory, following the linked prose retelling. The calm composition lets an intimate exchange interrupt the gathering’s public spectacle.","s303":"The impossible turns","s304":"One voice. One last effort.","s305":"The struggle lasts into the night. Exhausted, Koshoy nearly falls asleep as Joloy lifts him. Manas’s shout rouses him; he plants his feet and throws his opponent.","s306":"The final panel compresses that reversal into a single sweeping diagonal. Dust and cloth follow the giant’s movement. What looked immovable in the first image is suddenly airborne.","s307":"Compare Joloy’s upright silhouette in panel one with the turning figure here. This is an artistic condensation of the long bout, with pale paper and dust keeping the decisive movement legible.","s308":"The road out of Talas","s309":"After the death of Manas","s310":"Kanykey’s home has become dangerous. With Manas’s mother, Chiyrdy, she takes the infant Semetey toward Bukhara, the land of her father Temir Khan. They begin the escape on foot, carrying the child between them.","s311":"The opening panel leaves the gathering crowds behind. Two women, a bundle of cloth, and a long road fill the frame. Kanykey’s crimson coat becomes a small, stubborn point of warmth against the darkening steppe.","s312":"The child is the center of the composition even though he is its smallest figure. The women’s closeness gives the empty landscape its scale: this journey begins with mutual care.","s313":"A friend at the river","s314":"The Syr Darya crossing","s315":"The travelers reach a river they cannot cross. Bakai finds them and helps them to the far bank, carrying Semetey while Kanykey and Chiyrdy ride his horse. He then shelters them and searches for food.","s316":"The elder introduced among Manas’s companions returns here as a protector. Our panel stretches the river across the page, following the current toward his steady figure and the child held above the water.","s317":"Bakai’s long white beard, felt kalpak, and brown embroidered coat repeat his earlier portrait. The wide river panel makes crossing the page feel like crossing an obstacle.","s318":"A guardian in white","s319":"The wonder at Bayterek","s320":"At sacred Bayterek, the exhausted women fall asleep. A white argali ewe approaches Semetey’s cradle and feeds him. Kanykey wakes to find him missing, then discovers him safe with the animal at dawn; the ewe vanishes as she approaches.","s321":"This illustration imagines the moment before the feeding. A pale animal, a cradle, and sleeping travelers form a quiet pause in the journey. Here the epic allows help to arrive from beyond the human world.","s322":"The argali is a female wild mountain sheep, shown with smaller horns. The pale dawn and sheltering tree are artistic framing for the extraordinary encounter described in this prose version.","s323":"A future kept alive","s324":"Refuge with Kanykey’s family","s325":"Near her childhood home, Kanykey is found by her brother Ismail. He recognizes the travelers, and she entrusts Semetey to his care. He brings them to Bukhara, where the family conceals the child’s parentage.","s326":"The final image rests on a difficult gesture: a mother placing her child in another person’s arms so he can have a future. The open hands answer the protective embrace in the first panel. Survival has made another beginning possible.","s327":"The orchard setting recalls the lakeside meeting in the retelling. Indigo, previously the color of the threatening landscape, becomes the color of Ismail’s welcoming figure.","s328":"Kökötöy’s feast · The duel","s329":"Kökötöy’s feast · The elder & the giant","s330":"Return to the beginning","s331":"Reduced motion is enabled in your system settings","s332":"Resume decorative motion","s333":"Resume motion","metaTitle":"МАНАС — A people. A hero. An eternal story.","metaDescription":"Enter the world of Manas: a visual journey through the Kyrgyz epic, its forty comrades, three generations, and living oral tradition.","metaImage":"Manas and his mounted companions"}